-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Checks work similarly to a toggle button, however they're displayed differently, being represented as two separate
---elements - a label, and a toggleable button.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprite must represent a
---spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout using the following order - `unticked`,
---`unticked + mouseover`, `unticked + pressed`, `unticked + disabled`, `ticked`, `ticked + mouseover`, `ticked +
---pressed`, `ticked + disabled`.
---@class ui.Check : ui.Component
---@field label string Text to display as this check's label, aliases `text.content`.
---@field value boolean Indicates if the check is currently ticked or not.
---@field alignment ui.CheckAlignMode Determines how the Check's label and button should be positioned. Defaults to `ui.CheckAlignMode.LEFT`
---@field buttonSize integer Determines the size of the Check's button in interface units. Limited to a maximum of 255 units. Defaults to the component's height if not set, or set to 0.
---@field text ui.TextData Check label parameters.
---@field sprite ui.SpriteData Check sprite parameters.
ui.Check = {}

---Creates a new check on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this check in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Check # The newly created check. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Check.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Specifies how the contents of a check component should be positioned.
---@enum ui.CheckAlignMode
ui.CheckAlignMode = {
    ---Contents are aligned to the left and the button appears after the label.
    INLINE = 0,
    ---Contents are aligned to the right and the button appears before the label.
    INLINE_INVERTED = 2,
    ---Contents are aligned to the left and the button appears before the label.
    LEFT = -1,
    ---Contents are aligned to the right and the button appears after the label.
    RIGHT = 1,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.CheckAlignMode.FromID(ui.CheckAlignMode.INLINE)` is `"INLINE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.CheckAlignMode.FromID(value) end
